        "image_3": "as_3x5_clay",
        "heading": "How we started",
        "text": "<p>Wenlow Community Kitchen started in a church hall in 2009 with one soup pot and six volunteers. Today we run a choice pantry, cook a free lunch twice a week and deliver groceries to neighbours who can't get out.</p><p>Anyone who lives in Wenlow or the river villages is welcome. There are no forms, and nobody asks why you came.</p>",
        "link_label": "",
        "link": ""
      },
